# Trivy ignore list — accepted OS base-image findings.
#
# Every ID below is an OS package vulnerability from the Debian "trixie" base
# image with NO upstream fix available (Trivy `FixedVersion` is empty) as of
# 2026-06-14. They are accepted, not fixed, on the following grounds:
#
#   1. No fix exists — there is nothing to upgrade to.
#   2. Fathometer is a single-user, self-hosted, air-gap-first application
#      (no multi-tenant exposure, no untrusted local users on the host).
#   3. The affected package is not reachable by attacker-controlled input in
#      the app's request path (see per-group rationale below).
#
# SCOPE IS INTENTIONALLY NARROW: only the specific IDs listed here are
# suppressed. Any NEW CVE — including a new unfixable one — is deliberately
# NOT covered and will surface in CI and the Security tab. That is the point:
# keep the signal, drop the known-and-evaluated noise.
#
# REVIEW: drop an entry (and rebuild on a newer base) once an upstream fix
# lands, or re-evaluate the whole list if the threat model changes (e.g. the
# app stops being single-user / air-gap-first). Stale entries are harmless —
# a fixed package simply no longer matches.

# --- perl-base ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The Perl files are physically removed from the runtime image at build time
# (`rm -rf .../perl-base` in the runtime-builder stage); only the dpkg metadata
# entry remains, which is what Trivy keys off. No Perl interpreter is present
# or invoked at runtime, so these are effectively not-present findings.
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48959
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-9538
CVE-2026-48961
CVE-2026-7010
CVE-2025-15649
CVE-2011-4116

# --- curl / libcurl4t64 ------------------------------------------------------
# curl exists in the image solely for the container HEALTHCHECK, which hits a
# fixed local URL (http://127.0.0.1:8000/readyz). It is never invoked on
# attacker-controlled URLs or data. The app's own outbound traffic (LLM calls,
# optional research-worker) uses the Python httpx/openai stack, not libcurl.
CVE-2026-5773
CVE-2026-6276
CVE-2026-7168
CVE-2026-6429
CVE-2026-6253
CVE-2026-5545
CVE-2026-4873
CVE-2026-3805
CVE-2026-3784
CVE-2026-3783
CVE-2026-1965
CVE-2025-15224
CVE-2025-15079
CVE-2025-14819
CVE-2025-14524
CVE-2025-14017
CVE-2025-10966

# --- ncurses (ncurses-base/bin, libtinfo6, libncursesw6) ---------------------
# Terminal/TTY handling library. Fathometer is a headless Gunicorn web server;
# it parses no terminfo and processes no terminal escape sequences from request
# input. Not reachable over HTTP.
CVE-2025-69720
CVE-2025-6141

# --- libsqlite3-0 ------------------------------------------------------------
# The application uses PostgreSQL exclusively for all request-path data. SQLite
# is linked transitively (Python stdlib) but never opens attacker-controlled
# database files, so the parser CVEs are not reachable.
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824
CVE-2025-70873
CVE-2021-45346

# --- libssh2-1t64 ------------------------------------------------------------
# SSH client library pulled in transitively (via libcurl). The app initiates no
# SSH connections.
CVE-2026-7598

# --- krb5 (libgssapi-krb5-2, libk5crypto3, libkrb5-3, libkrb5support0) --------
# Kerberos client libraries linked transitively (libcurl/ldap). The app
# performs no Kerberos/GSSAPI authentication.
CVE-2026-11850
CVE-2024-26461
CVE-2024-26458
CVE-2018-5709

# --- libldap2 ----------------------------------------------------------------
# LDAP client linked transitively (via libcurl). The app performs no LDAP
# queries.
CVE-2026-22185
CVE-2020-15719
CVE-2017-17740
CVE-2017-14159
CVE-2015-3276

# --- glibc (libc6, libc-bin) -------------------------------------------------
# Core C library. The flagged CVEs concern regex/printf/iconv edge cases driven
# by locally crafted inputs to those specific APIs; none are exposed to remote,
# attacker-controlled input in this app. Several are decade-old, disputed, or
# explicitly low-impact entries.
CVE-2026-6238
CVE-2026-5928
CVE-2026-5450
CVE-2026-5435
CVE-2019-9192
CVE-2019-1010025
CVE-2019-1010024
CVE-2019-1010023
CVE-2019-1010022
CVE-2018-20796
CVE-2010-4756

# --- util-linux family (bsdutils, libblkid1, libmount1, libsmartcols1, -------
#     libuuid1, liblastlog2-2, mount, login, util-linux) ----------------------
# Disk/mount/login utilities. The container mounts no filesystems at runtime
# and runs as a single fixed non-root user; these tools are not invoked on
# request input.
CVE-2026-27456
CVE-2026-3184
